  "worked_solution": "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.025t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial value of the car.\n\nWe are given that the value in $2016$ was $$62\\,000.$ So, substituting $t=6$ and $P(6)=$62\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(6) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.025\\cdot 6} \\\\ 62\\,000 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.15} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{62\\,000}{{e}^{0.15}} \\\\  & \u224853\\,363.895,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.025t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the car's value $15$ years after $2010.$ So, substituting $t=15$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15) & =53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.025\\cdot 15} \\\\  & =53\\,363.895\\,{e}^{0.375} \\\\  & \u224877\\,644,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, the car's value in $2025$ will be $$77\\,644.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
